# Assignment 2.1 — First HTML Page

## Objective
To create a basic HTML webpage using HTML elements, headings, comments, and proper indentation.

## Solution

First, I created a file named `index.html` in Visual Studio Code. I used the `<!DOCTYPE html>` declaration to define the document as HTML5. Then, I added the `html`, `head`, and `body` elements to structure the webpage.

I set the page title to **My First Webpage** using the `title` element inside the `head` section. In the `body` section, I added one main heading using the `h1` element and four subheadings using the `h2` element. I also added paragraphs to provide information under each heading.

I used HTML comments to describe the different sections of the code and maintained proper indentation to make the code easy to read and understand. Finally, I saved the file and opened it in a web browser to verify that the webpage displayed correctly.

## HTML Code

Save the following code in a file named `index.html`.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">

    <!-- Page title -->
    <title>My First Webpage</title>
</head>
<body>

    <!-- Main heading -->
    <h1>Welcome to My First Webpage</h1>

    <!-- First subheading -->
    <h2>About Me</h2>
    <p>Hello! I am learning HTML and web development.</p>

    <!-- Second subheading -->
    <h2>My Education</h2>
    <p>I am learning how to create webpages using HTML.</p>

    <!-- Third subheading -->
    <h2>My Hobbies</h2>
    <p>My hobbies include reading, listening to music, and learning new skills.</p>

    <!-- Fourth subheading -->
    <h2>My Goals</h2>
    <p>My goal is to become a skilled web developer.</p>

</body>
</html>
```

## Result

The HTML webpage was created successfully. The browser displayed the page title as "My First Webpage" and showed one main heading, four subheadings, and their respective paragraphs.

## Conclusion

This assignment helped me understand the basic structure of an HTML document and the use of headings, paragraphs, comments, and the title element. I also learned how to save an HTML file and open it in a web browser.

